From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taynotfound <marztayron@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rain-1024: tell the PMIC what PS_HOLD low means (real power-off)

Power off came back as a reboot even unplugged: the bootloader leaves
PON PS_HOLD_RESET_CTL at warm reset, and PSCI SYSTEM_OFF only drops
PS_HOLD. Warm reboots also keep the Wi-Fi chip powered in a state its
firmware rejects (wlfw cap err 119 on every boot after the first).
haltRestart now sets the reset type first through the PON owner channel
(as Linux qpnp_pon_system_pwr_off): shutdown for power off, hard reset
(rails cycled) for restart.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
index 080552c..0df049a 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
@@ -249,4 +249,25 @@ sweet_keys_init(void)
 		printf("SWEET KEYS: kernel_thread_start failed %d\n", kr);
 	}
 }
+/*
+ * rain: what the PMIC does when PS_HOLD drops (PON PS_HOLD_RESET_CTL 0x85a, enable in CTL2 0x85b bit 7;
+ * Linux qpnp_pon_system_pwr_off, PM6125 gen2 PON). The bootloader leaves it at warm reset, so PSCI
+ * SYSTEM_OFF came back as a reboot, and warm reboots keep the Wi-Fi chip powered in a state its
+ * firmware rejects (wlfw cap err 119). type: 0x04 shutdown, 0x07 hard reset (rails cycled), 0x01 warm.
+ * Called from SweetPlatformExpert::haltRestart just before PSCI. Returns 0 when all three writes landed.
+ */
+int sweet_pon_ps_hold(unsigned type);
+int
+sweet_pon_ps_hold(unsigned type)
+{
+	uint8_t check = 0;
+	bool ok = keys_write(keys_pon_apid, 0x085bu, 0x00);     /* disable before changing the type */
+	delay(100);                                             /* >= 3 sleep-clock cycles */
+	ok = ok && keys_write(keys_pon_apid, 0x085au, (uint8_t)type);
+	ok = ok && keys_write(keys_pon_apid, 0x085bu, 0x80);
+	bool r = keys_read(keys_pon_apid, 0x085au, &check);
+	printf("RAIN PON: PS_HOLD reset type %#x: %s (reads back %#x, %d)\n", type, ok ? "set" : "FAILED", check, r);
+	return ok ? 0 : -1;
+}
+
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
index 397f1f5..b734d2b 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetPlatformExpert.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ public:
 
 extern "C" int sweet_spmi_init(void);
 extern "C" vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t phys_addr, vm_size_t size);
+extern "C" int sweet_pon_ps_hold(unsigned type);
 extern "C" int sweet_spmi_read(unsigned sid, unsigned addr, uint8_t *out);
 
 /*
@@ -90,6 +91,8 @@ SweetPlatformExpert::haltRestart(unsigned int type)
 	} else {
 		return IODTPlatformExpert::haltRestart(type);
 	}
+	/* rain: the PMIC must be told first, or PS_HOLD low is a warm reset either way */
+	sweet_pon_ps_hold(fn == 0x84000008u ? 0x04 : 0x07);
 	IOLog("RAIN: %s via PSCI\n", fn == 0x84000008u ? "power off" : "restart");
 	__asm__ volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
 	register uint64_t x0 __asm__("x0") = fn;
